\paragraph{Scale invariance and optimization diagnostics.}
Because affine invariance is a standard Nash-bargaining property rather than a new alignment theorem, Table~\ref{tab:uf-scale-covariance} checks whether the implemented update preserves it numerically. For each frozen response pair, we compare the sign of the aggregation-induced policy-update score before and after independently rescaling the objective coordinates. \NBPO{} changes this direction for only $0.01\%$ of pairs; alternative fixed-weight or maxmin rules change more often. Appendix~\ref{app:optimization-diagnostics} reports temperature, comparator-sampling, fixed-point, dual, and regression diagnostics needed to identify the remaining gap between the population objective and the neural implementation.

