Table~\ref{tab:objectivewise-appendix} gives the objective-wise decomposition of the existing
game-surplus results. Its \NBPO{} row comes from an earlier campaign that fitted the policy with
the pipeline's RONPO-style regression rather than the sampled pair target of
\eqref{eq:binary-target} and \eqref{eq:regression-loss}. That arm is a different objective, not a
differently tuned \NBPO{}: it optimises a RONPO-style regression rather than the finite-pool target
of \eqref{eq:binary-target-mean} and \eqref{eq:regression-loss}, so no setting of $\eta_t$
reproduces it. It is therefore kept only as the historical diagnostic it is, and every \NBPO{} row
in the main text is a matched finite-pool fit. These values are useful for diagnosing which objectives each policy sacrifices, but they are defined by the adaptive game evaluation introduced by NBPO and are therefore secondary to the common external metric in Table~\ref{tab:neutral-objectivewise}.

